# Final objective: actual recommendation hit rate

- Always follow the prediction research objective in root `AGENTS.md`.
- Optimize actual settled recommended picks, not merely Brier/log loss, xG, PA outcomes, or data volume.
- Show hits/settled picks, recommendation count/coverage, pushes/voids/unsettled, dates, leagues and sports.
- Compare unchanged selection rules and matched counts on the same games; disclose odds mix and added/removed picks.
- Distinguish current production, market and research baselines. Never substitute a proxy baseline silently.
- No future-data leakage, post-kickoff pick revisions, or selecting a winner on a repeatedly reused test set and calling it confirmed.
- Execute bounded experiments when asked, record failures too, and reserve untouched chronological validation.
- Save research outputs as private SQLite and Markdown. No scheduled continuation or visual app unless requested.
- No guarantee of higher accuracy, and no unverified production adoption.
